Let~$K$ be a number field such that ${\mathcal A}\subset K$. For~$\alpha\in{\mathcal A}$ and~$v\in M_K$, we let \[ \alpha_v =  egin{cases} \alpha&	ext{if $\|\alpha\|_v\le1$,}\ \alpha^{-1}&	ext{if $\|\alpha\|_v>1$,}\ \end{cases} \] so in particular $\|\alpha_v\|_v\le 1$. We now compute  egin{align} (n\log m)\Delta({\mathcal A},m,n) &= \sum_{\alpha\in{\mathcal A}}\sum_{v\mid m} v(\alpha^n-1) &&	ext{def. of $\Delta({\mathcal A},m,n)$,} 
otag\ &\le \sum_{\alpha\in{\mathcal A}}\sum_{v\in M_K^0} v(\alpha^n-1) &&	ext{since $\alpha\in ar\mathbb{Z}$,} 
otag\ &= \sum_{\alpha\in{\mathcal A}}\sum_{v\in M_K^\infty} \log\|\alpha^n-1\|_v &&	ext{product rule,} 
otag\ &\le \sum_{\alpha\in{\mathcal A}}\sum_{\substack{v\in M_K^\infty\\|\alpha\|_v>1\}} \log\|\alpha^n\|_v + \sum_{\alpha\in{\mathcal A}}\sum_{v\in M_K^\infty} \log\|\alpha_v^n-1\|_v \hidewidth 
otag\ &= n\sum_{\alpha\in{\mathcal A}} h(\alpha) + \sum_{\alpha\in{\mathcal A}}\sum_{v\in M_K^\infty} \log\|\alpha_v^n-1\|_v. \hidewidth \end{align} We now replace~${\mathcal A}$ with~${\mathcal A}^j$. Then using $h(\alpha^j)=jh(\alpha)$ and Proposition~ef{prop:DAjmngeDAmn}, which says that $\Delta({\mathcal A},m,n)\le\Delta({\mathcal A}^j,m,n)$, we find that \[ (n\log m)\Delta({\mathcal A},m,n) \le nj\sum_{\alpha\in{\mathcal A}}h(\alpha) + \sum_{\alpha\in{\mathcal A}}\sum_{v\in M_K^\infty} \log\|\alpha_v^{jn}-1\|_v . \] We multiply by the Fej'er multiplier $1- rac{j}{J+1}$ and sum over $1\le j\le J$ to obtain  egin{multline*}  rac{Jn\log m}{2}\Delta({\mathcal A},m,n) \le  rac{(J^2+2J)n}{6}\sum_{\alpha\in{\mathcal A}}h(\alpha) \* + \sum_{\alpha\in{\mathcal A}}\sum_{v\in M_K^\infty} \sum_{j=1}^J \left(1- rac{j}{J+1}ight)\log\|\alpha_v^{jn}-1\|_v . \end{multline*} Note that the sum over~$v$ is over archimedean absolute values, so if we assume that~$\alpha_v$ is chosen in the unit disk to maximize the innermost sum over~$j$, we get the estimate  egin{multline*}  rac{Jn\log m}{2}\Delta({\mathcal A},m,n) \* \le  rac{(J^2+2J)n}{6}\sum_{\alpha\in{\mathcal A}}h(\alpha) + |{\mathcal A}| \sup_{\substack{z\in\mathbb{C}\|z|\le1\}} \sum_{j=1}^J \left(1- rac{j}{J+1}ight)\log|z^j-1|. \end{multline*} We can now use Proposition~ef{prop:fejarestimate} to conclude that \[  rac{Jn\log m}{2}\Delta({\mathcal A},m,n) \le  rac{(J^2+2J)n}{6}\sum_{\alpha\in{\mathcal A}}h(\alpha) +  rac{|{\mathcal A}|}{2}\left(\log\left( rac{J}{2}+1ight)+1ight). \] After a little bit of algebra, we obtain the desired result.

